[     0.0s] A key of the form "<fmt> (record_inst)", e.g. "f16 (record_inst)", takes the same range syntax
[     0.0s] and additionally reports the specific instruction/source line that triggered each threshold hit,
[     0.0s] the same way exception reports do -- useful for root-causing how values reached a given range.
[     0.0s] 
[     0.0s] If "doublings" is N (N>0), every bin starts reporting every "count" occurrences; each time a
[     0.0s] bin reports, its own threshold doubles (count -> 2*count -> 4*count -> ...). After a bin has
[     0.0s] doubled N times, the NEXT report resets every bin in that kernel back to the starting "count"
[     0.0s] and 0 doublings, then the cycle repeats. "doublings": 0 (the default) disables this -- every
[     0.0s] bin just reports every "count" occurrences forever, as before.
